 "findings": [
  "Normal returns: monthly stocks show 23 moves beyond 3 standard deviations where a bell curve expects 5.0; the normal 1-in-100 month understates the real one by 30%.",
  "Brent has 24 daily moves beyond 5 standard deviations where a bell curve expects 0.01.",
  "Taleb's kappa for monthly stocks is 0.13: matching what 30 Gaussian months reveal about the mean takes about 39 months.",
  "The trend rule's Sharpe gain disappears at 56 basis points a switch, and by a four-month delay.",
  "Kelly sizing on stocks from a 30-year backtest ranged from 1.4 to 8.0 times capital depending on which 30 years: the edge is not known well enough to bet full Kelly.",
  "In 400 bootstrapped histories a 60/40 mix beats all stocks on Sharpe 88% of the time; in histories drawn from inflationary months, 4%."
 ]
